> 1) How important is it to have a really good weapon? I have Cleaver at the
> mo, but the selection spoilers don't seem to like it much. The problem is
> that I've seen about 7 artifacts this game, so wishing won't be very fun.
> And I've used up all /o create monster trying to get a different one. The
> only other one I've found that I like the look of is Magicbane. So if I
> just bless one of these up should that be good enough? (And which one
> should I used?)

Well, you didn't say what the other artifacts were, so I assume they are 
all useless banes and such. Cleaver is a two-handed weapon, which is 
bad, because it could get cursed (either from the random malignant aura, 
or from the Wizard or other spellcaster casting it), and that would be 
Very Bad. Also, you cannot twoweapon with it. Magicbane in a good choice 
on the ascension run because it will nullify cursing attacks 95% of the 
time when wielded. Of course, it doesn't do near as much damage as 
Cleaver, but you could make up for it by twoweaponing, even if you only 
enchant Magicbane to +2. Also, on the ascension run, you shouldn't spend 
much time fighting anyway.

> 2) I have no =oFree action. Should I use a wish to get one or just save all
> my wishes (of which I have at least 5) for wishing for blessed cockatrice
> corpses for beating the wizard with?

I don't know why you would want one for fighting the Wizard (according 
to the spoiler, magic resistance has the same effect as free action with 
regard to the spell Paralyze), but it's generally a good idea to have 
anyway. As for wizard-killing devices, if you're willing to wish for 
stuff, you're better off wishing either for a wand of death, or for 
rings of poly and poly control, so you can lay a bunch of cockatrice 
eggs (wield them so you won't waste them if you miss).

> 3) When fighting the wizzard is it safe to wear my "o reflection or should I
> keep life saving on just to be carefull? (I have no other means of
> reflection at the mo).

The Wizard will not instakill you if you don't have reflection (only 
magic resistance protects against the touch of death), but I think he 
could possibly cast Lightning, which could blow up your rings/wands if 
you don't have reflection. Also, for just wearing the amulet normally, 
most people recommend choosing reflection rather than life saving.



